<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Slurs on grace notes, read as slurs (as osmd-dart test/grace_slur_beam_single_number_time_test.dart).
     m1: a slur from the first of two grace notes over their main note to the last note of the measure
         (Couperin, Concerts royaux II Air tendre m34).
     m2: grace notes slurred to their own main notes (the group's arc), then an unslurred grace note (Air tendre m12).
     m3: a slur from a beamed grace pair to its own main note D6 that also ends the slur from the chord before
         (Bowen, Viola Sonata No. 2 I m221).
     m4: a slur from a main note to its after-grace note (Couperin, Concerts royaux IV Rigaudon m22).
     m5, m6: slurs reusing number 1 before and after a grace note's slur of that number, and one over an unslurred grace note.
     m7: a grace slur start without a stop (keeps the group's arc). -->
